Subject: [PATCH 2/8] aarch64: fix rhs-alias-into-dest ALU ops for any lhs home

When an ALU op's destination register was assigned the same machine
register as the rhs operand's home, emit_int_binop_impl materialized the
rhs AFTER writing dest, clobbering it (x86 two-address hazard, ARM side).
The old fix only handled lhs-in-dest; generalize: whenever rhs-home ==
dest-home, move lhs into place (operand_to_x0 when lhs itself aliases
dest, plain operand otherwise) and emit 'op dest, x0|w0, rhs'.
arm_csinc_select -O2 is GCC-exact again.
---
 src/backend/arm/codegen/alu.rs | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

