From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] vectorize: require canonical unit-stride GEP offsets
 (struct_stride fix)

gep_uses_iv accepted ANY offset that merely depended on the IV, but the
reduction transform models accesses as invariant_base + iv*elem_size,
re-scales the offset chain by vec_width and (byte-IV path) relatches the
IV in bytes. For struct streams (arr[i].i, byte stride 12) that model is
wrong three ways at once:

- find_reduction_byte_iv's Shl arm matched shl(mul(sext(i),12),2) as a
  'byte IV' (misidentified stride-48 IV),
- the vector body loaded elem_size*vec_width CONTIGUOUS bytes while the
  elements actually span stride*vec_width (n=4: 1+2+3+4=10 instead of
  22; q-register gather over adjacent struct fields),
- the synthesized scalar remainder loop discarded the original offset
  expression and re-addressed with i_rem*elem_size (i*4 instead of i*12;
  n=3: 1+2+3=6 instead of 12),
- with a dynamic limit the byte-IV bound rewrite produced
  udiv(n,4)*48 against an IV still stepping +1: the vector loop ran
  n/4*48 iterations for n>=4 (out-of-bounds reads; latent, the n=3
  regression only showed the remainder path).

Fix: gep_uses_iv takes the element size and now requires the canonical
unit-stride shape iv*elem_size / (cast iv)*elem_size /
(cast iv)<<log2(elem_size) via a strict iterative matcher
(offset_is_canonical_unit_stride + scaled_operand_is_iv); raw-iv
offsets, iv_derived shapes (iv+1), narrowing casts and any other
derivation fail closed to the scalar loop. value_depends_on_iv (now
unused) is removed. Thread elem_size through all 10 call sites
(reduction sum/cast/dot, secondary accumulators, map dst/src - map
already had the byte-IV gate, now gep_uses_iv agrees).

aggregate_dse_soundness (struct_array_sum) passes; -O0..-O3 correct;
ARM regression 359/44/75.
