From ff1c06049c1fa2b3b28bc0b057ffd1453f4b43f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:54:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] aarch64: complete NEON vector-intrinsic coverage (i64
 reductions were silently wrong)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

emit_intrinsic_arm silently no-op'd any Vec intrinsic without a NEON
arm. Three consequences, all observed:

- VecLoadI64x2 lowered to NOTHING: the i64 reduction loop accumulated
  v17 uninitialized (vectorize_sum_i64* family: rc=1, wrong sums).
- VecMulI64x2 emitted 'mul v.2d', which does not exist in AArch64 NEON
  (assembler error). Expand per 64-bit lane through GPRs (umov/mul/mov
  v.d[i]); wrapping i64 multiply is exactly 'mul x,x,x'. Scratch is
  confined to x0/x9; q0/q1 operands stay intact per lane. Differential
  wraparound stress (2^62-scale products) is GCC-exact.
- The 128-bit map/stencil forms (VecSub/Div/Sqrt F64x2|F32x4,
  VecBroadcastI64x2, VecZeroF32x4, VecHorizontalAddF32x4, VecStore/
  VecLoadI64x2) had no lowering either — one transform-match away from
  the same silent-drop class. All implemented (fsub/fdiv/fsqrt .2d/.4s,
  dup .2d from x0, eor zero, addv s0 horizontal).

Every remaining Vec op (AVX2/x8 shapes and the widening adds) now hits
an explicit unimplemented! naming the op — an x86-only shape leaking
past the vectorizer target gate is a loud ICE, never wrong code.

ARM regression 368/37/75 (was 360/45/75); lib tests 1270/0/6.
