Subject: [PATCH 8/8] docs: S06 follow-up - f128 carrier AAPCS64 fix, open
 peephole global-carrier bug + RISC-V gp-pair arm

---
 updates/followup_2026-08-28_session09.md | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/updates/followup_2026-08-28_session09.md b/updates/followup_2026-08-28_session09.md
index 7431164b..0d1ba3ae 100644
--- a/updates/followup_2026-08-28_session09.md
+++ b/updates/followup_2026-08-28_session09.md
@@ -116,3 +116,32 @@ are rejected with precise messages.
 APPLIES-CLEAN (validated with `git apply --check` on a pristine base
 worktree), zero garbage (no eprintln!/dbg!/TRACE/env-gated probes added;
 the pre-existing `resolve_pending_instructions` warning path untouched).
+
+## S06 — _Float128 carrier (IrType::U128) AAPCS64 fix — COMMITTED f66a5905 (7th commit)
+
+Root cause was never the flag plumbing (verified both sides via CCC_DUMP_IR): classify_args_core
+emitted x86-only CoreArgClass::F128SseReg unconditionally, and ARM ignored it plus ret_is_f128_sse.
+Fix (all validated, x86 byte-identical):
+- call_abi.rs: per-target classification, gated config.f128_in_fp_regs (ARM-only) -> F128FpReg/F128Stack.
+- ARM: func/call_ret_is_f128_sse stash; return path loads carrier into q0 (slot-direct fast path,
+  OverAligned/Reg fallbacks); call-result store intercepts with single `str q0`.
+- Caller staging: U128-typed F128Reg var-args load the source slot directly; IrConst::I128 consts
+  stage bit-exactly (to_f64() integer-converted 1.5F128's bits into ~8.5e37).
+Results: lib 1270/0/6 exact; ARM 371/34F/75S (was 369/36F, no regressions); x86 535/5F identical
+with and without the change (all 5 pre-existing); f1/f2/f3 GCC-oracle parity ident=1.50 add3=4.50 mix=10.6875.
+
+### Open, in order (paused mid-investigation this session)
+1. ARM peephole miscompiles GLOBAL-scope carrier loads: `mov x9,x20; ldr x0,[x9]; ldr x1,[x9,#8]`
+   loses the mov while only ONE use is rewritten -> `ldr x0,[x0]; ldr x1,[x9,#8]` (stale x9, SIGSEGV).
+   Repro /tmp/wd/f5g.c (global _Float128 g=42.0F128; printf((double)g)). Verified NOT
+   eliminate_move_chains/eliminate_unused_x9_address_moves/propagate_address_aliases/
+   eliminate_overwritten_moves in isolation (stepwise unit test). Next suspect:
+   late propagate_register_copies (rewrites only the single next instruction) followed by a
+   move-deletion pass (eliminate_dead_call_staging_moves?) that then sees x9 as unused.
+   This is PRE-EXISTING (U128 global loads predate the carrier work) and is what still fails
+   f128_softfloat (rc=139).
+2. RISC-V: same carrier bug class — call_abi.rs needs `config.f128_in_gp_pairs` -> F128GpPair arm
+   (variant exists, consumed at riscv calls.rs:46). _Float128 on RISC-V is broken today.
+3. Then remaining ARM fails: vex_move_false_dep (DIFFER), va_arg_wide_struct (rc=1),
+   cast_chain_fold, nested_functions, glibc_vstmxcsr audit; then xarch census porting.
+
